title: PostgreSQL 19 introduces concurrent table repacking and replication upgrades
source: hn
url: https://www.pgedge.com/blog/postgresql-19-is-here-worth-the-wait
date: '2026-11-22'
authors:
- Ahsan Hadi
why_read: Read this to understand the practical operational improvements in PostgreSQL 19, focusing on non-blocking table repacks and streamlined logical replication.
hn_id: '50597961'
comments: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50597961
image: /infographics/02-hn-50597961.jpg
---

Online table compaction in PostgreSQL has historically required dangerous trade-offs or brittle third-party extensions. Running a standard VACUUM FULL takes an exclusive lock on the table, blocking incoming transactions and often causing downtime on high-throughput services.

PostgreSQL 19 addresses this operational bottleneck by introducing native REPACK with the CONCURRENTLY option. In real-world benchmarks, tables were rebuilt in under a second while sustaining continuous write workloads of over 2,000 inserts per second without transaction failures. The rebuild requires a primary key or replica identity index and executes concurrently without locking out reads or writes.

Logical replication also receives a substantial overhaul: sequences can now be synchronized natively using ALL SEQUENCES and REFRESH SEQUENCES, eliminating manual setval scripts during migrations. Furthermore, logical replication can be enabled dynamically without a server restart when wal_level is already set to replica.

For database reliability and operational maintenance, these primitives dramatically lower the friction of live migrations and routine maintenance.

