Running 500B+ parameter Mixture of Experts models at low latencies requires squeezing every cycle out of the GPU tensor cores. Standard frameworks like vLLM provide solid baselines, but generic implementations often leave significant performance on the table when novel hardware instructions arrive.

RightNow AI benchmarked custom CUDA kernels for Inkling 2 Small (a 594B MoE) across 8 NVIDIA B300 GPUs. They implemented layers 0 through 39 on Blackwell block-scaled FP4 tensor cores and layers 40 through 47 on MXFP8 cores. The result was a 5.1x speedup on NVFP4 expert GEMMs and 7.5x on MXFP8 expert GEMMs compared to baseline kernels, while maintaining bit-identical outputs and matching log-probabilities within 0.025 nats.

